<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌣 LIVE UV INDEX</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/uv_index/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>UV Index (UV Index), fixed absolute scale: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (green, low) → 3-5 (yellow, moderate) → 6-7 (orange, high) → 8-10 (red, very high) → <b>HIGHEST+ 11+</b> (violet, extreme). Same index always shows the same color. Current maximum over the lakes: <b>3.1</b>.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP CPC Global UV Index, operational GRIB2 (12 UTC GFS run, hourly steps to 120 h)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌣 LIVE UV INDEX — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_UV_Index.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>3600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
